# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit the plaintext learner records.
#
# private/learners.source.js holds every name, password and queue in
# the clear. If it is in the repo then js/data/learners.js may as well
# not be encrypted at all, because the passwords that decrypt it are
# sitting next to it.
#
# Adding this file does NOT remove anything already committed. If
# private/ is currently tracked, run this once:
#
#     git rm -r --cached private
#     git commit -m "Stop tracking private/"
#
# And note that git history keeps the old copies. Anything that has
# ever been pushed should be treated as exposed — change the passwords
# rather than assuming removal was enough.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
private/
*.source.js


# Anything else with secrets in it
.env
.env.*
secrets*
*.key
*.pem


# Scratch files that should not travel
*.bak
*.orig
*.tmp
*~
draft-*
scratch/
notes-private/


# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-workspace
*.code-workspace


# Operating systems
